 "final_result": "Built a complete three-script DFT workflow for zincblende GaAs from scratch.\n\n**Materials Project ID:** mp-2534, space group F-43m (#216).\n\n**Atom count:** 2 atoms before and after primitive-cell reduction (the MP CIF was already primitive; seekpath confirmed F-43m #216).\n\n**Workflow outline:**\n1. `reduce_primitive.py` \u2014 fetched GaAs CIF, reduced to primitive cell via chem_llm.kpath (kp_atoms(standard_kpath(atoms))).\n2. `generate_structures.py` \u2014 generated 51 structures (structure_000.cif unperturbed + 50 perturbed with 300 K thermal displacements: U_Ga=0.005 A\u00b2, U_As=0.003 A\u00b2, plus ~1% random diagonal strain). GaAs is stable at room temperature; heavier As moves less than Ga.\n3. `setup_jobs.py` \u2014 for each structure, created calculations/NNN/ with pseudopotentials, kpath.json, pw.in (SCF), bands.in (NSCF), and bands_post.in (bands.x). Used write_espresso_in with the primitive cell from kp_atoms(kp), SCF k-mesh from scf_kmesh(prim, metal=False) = 8\u00d78\u00d78, and bands k-points from kp_kpts(kp).\n4. `plot_bands.py` \u2014 plotted the band structure for calculations/000 using chem_llm.kpath.plot_axis and chem_llm.qe_output.read_pw_out/band_edges, aligned to VBM.\n\n**ASE functions used:** ase.io.read/write (CIF I/O), ase.io.espresso.write_espresso_in (QE input files), ase.Atoms (structure representation). No pymatgen imported.\n\n**Band gap obtained:** 0.075 eV (PBEsol, scalar-relativistic, 114 Ry cutoff, 8\u00d78\u00d78 k-mesh). VBM = 8.939 eV, CBM = 9.014 eV (absolute, before VBM alignment).\n\n**Scientific assumptions:**\n- Scalar-relativistic pseudopotentials (Ga Z=31, As Z=33, both < 54; no spin-orbit physics targeted).\n- PBEsol functional (stringent, norm-conserving, Pseudo-Dojo).\n- ecutwfc = 114 Ry (from Ga's 57 Ha \u00d7 2, the larger of Ga/As); ecutrho = 456 Ry.\n- Fixed occupations (GaAs is a semiconductor, not a metal).\n- nbnd = 44 (2\u00d7 occupied bands of 22, from z_valence: Ga=21, As=23, total 44 electrons).\n- 300 K thermal displacements with U_Ga=0.005 A\u00b2, U_As=0.003 A\u00b2 (heavier As moves less).\n\n**Needs expert review:** The computed band gap of 0.075 eV is much smaller than the experimental 1.42 eV. This is expected for PBEsol (which underestimates gaps) but the value is unusually small even for PBEsol. The semicore states (Ga 3d, As 3s/3p) included in the pseudopotentials (z_valence=21 for Ga, 23 for As) may affect the gap. A hybrid functional (HSE06) or GW correction would be needed for a quantitatively accurate gap.",
